  "name": "seL4",
  "description": "seL4 is a high-performance microkernel featuring a capability-based security model and the world's first machine-checked formal proof of functional correctness. It provides a foundation for secure, high-assurance systems by enforcing strict isolation and resource management across diverse hardware architectures, including ARM and x86. The implementation combines rigorous formal methods with highly optimized systems code to achieve both mathematical certainty of behavior and production-grade performance.",
